WEBVTT

00:03.194 --> 00:05.254
What are you wishing for?

00:11.544 --> 00:13.004
It's a secret.

00:13.674 --> 00:19.514
Those clear eyes stared straight forward,
showing not a hint of hesitation.

00:21.684 --> 00:26.454
I felt like within those eyes lay
the things that over time I had lost.

00:27.624 --> 00:29.184
And then...

00:29.824 --> 00:30.814
I, too...

00:36.704 --> 00:39.694
Something reached for but cannot be grasped...

00:41.034 --> 00:44.664
Something that strays from that hand,
going far away...

00:46.404 --> 00:51.004
People will always pursue such things.

00:52.044 --> 00:54.774
And before long, become lost.

01:01.354 --> 01:05.794
This is our story of one such summer.

01:23.644 --> 01:25.084
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

01:25.084 --> 01:28.754
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow
Asphalt ni saita

01:28.754 --> 01:29.214
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

01:29.514 --> 01:33.184
Kodomo no rakugaki ga

01:33.954 --> 01:37.584
Kagerou ni yurarete

01:38.424 --> 01:41.264
Arukidashita

01:41.394 --> 01:46.234
Daremo shiranai yakusoku no

01:46.234 --> 01:49.864
Oka de meguriau

01:50.404 --> 01:55.114
Tatta ichido no kyou to iu

01:55.114 --> 01:59.884
Kiseki no toki wo kanjite

01:59.884 --> 02:04.054
Nagareru kumo oikakete

02:04.054 --> 02:08.394
Imanimo tsukamesou na

02:08.394 --> 02:12.764
Mune no yokan takanari

02:12.764 --> 02:17.394
Ugokihajimeta unmei

02:17.504 --> 02:21.874
Me ga sameru hodo mabushii

02:21.874 --> 02:25.894
Asa no hi yorimo atatakai

02:26.144 --> 02:30.044
Owari no nai kagayaku

02:30.384 --> 02:37.684
Hikari no kisetsu ni dakarete

02:40.154 --> 02:44.284
To Be Here

02:49.194 --> 02:50.324
Karada is?

02:51.204 --> 02:54.364
She's in love with the boy.

02:55.074 --> 02:56.294
With Tetsu?

02:58.104 --> 02:59.044
She's with him.

02:59.674 --> 03:05.184
It looks like he still can't accept
that Karada's become an adult,

03:05.184 --> 03:07.844
but the point is, he found her.

03:08.714 --> 03:10.584
Beat you to the punch, huh?

03:13.494 --> 03:17.824
What is it? You look like a real big brother.

03:19.324 --> 03:20.724
I'm not sure.

03:21.194 --> 03:23.294
Just a normal kind of sadness.

03:24.364 --> 03:28.304
But he's taken the first step in a new direction.

03:29.174 --> 03:33.644
And I won't run away anymore, either.
Not from her.

03:33.644 --> 03:34.904
And I...

03:35.514 --> 03:38.604
I have something to apologize for.

03:48.454 --> 03:50.684
I... I'm Karada!

03:50.794 --> 03:54.594
Karada lokawa, the girl you tried to take
to see that river but couldn't!

03:55.734 --> 03:57.794
Dammit!

04:03.074 --> 04:04.764
U-um!

04:12.484 --> 04:13.914
Jeez!

04:13.914 --> 04:15.684
This may be hard, but that's not
the way to deal with it.

04:15.684 --> 04:16.054
Pension
ISOKA
This may be hard, but that's not
the way to deal with it.

04:16.054 --> 04:17.174
Pension
ISOKA

04:27.134 --> 04:27.964
Wait.

04:30.664 --> 04:32.694
Where's my sister?

04:33.164 --> 04:34.834
If you mean lokawa, I'm going out to look right...

04:34.834 --> 04:35.074
You've already found her.
If you mean lokawa, I'm going out to look right...

04:35.074 --> 04:36.094
You've already found her.

04:36.674 --> 04:38.074
What are you talking about?

04:38.444 --> 04:41.344
If you really care for my sister,
then please believe.

04:41.344 --> 04:42.504
Cut the crap already.

04:45.084 --> 04:49.014
Iokawa is super tiny! Like THIS!

04:49.354 --> 04:52.154
She... She can't be that grown-up!

04:53.324 --> 04:55.354
If you mean Miss Sato...

04:55.354 --> 04:59.354
There's a girl named "Sato"
at the bed and breakfast just up ahead.

05:02.094 --> 05:03.494
Wait.

05:08.434 --> 05:10.704
CIGARETTES

05:26.084 --> 05:30.384
Um, you said you wanted to talk?
I'm sort of in a hurry.

05:30.994 --> 05:33.654
Do you know of the Shiranui?

05:34.334 --> 05:38.204
In rural areas on the island of Kyushu,
there's a phenomenon called the Shiranui.

05:38.204 --> 05:41.764
Around this time, it appears as a
strange light visible at night.

05:42.534 --> 05:43.904
According to legend,

05:43.904 --> 05:46.374
the light beckons the Emperor Keiko,

05:46.374 --> 05:50.384
who 2,000 years ago engaged in the conquest
of Kyushu, causing him to roam certain...

05:50.384 --> 05:53.084
Um, I really am in a hurry.

05:53.084 --> 05:55.074
Come now, wait a moment.

05:55.614 --> 05:58.724
There are various theories regarding the light,

05:58.724 --> 06:02.224
but the most important thing is
that it continues to shine to this day,

06:02.224 --> 06:06.354
lighting the waterways and guiding the people.

06:06.924 --> 06:11.334
There are mysterious things in this world,
and people who believe in them.

06:11.904 --> 06:13.834
That's quite splendid, don't you think?

06:16.874 --> 06:19.744
Well, I just wanted you to know that story.

06:24.014 --> 06:26.084
Oh, by the way.

06:26.084 --> 06:29.984
Don't let anyone know I was out here fishing.

06:43.564 --> 06:44.934
I was happy.

06:45.764 --> 06:48.734
You've looked for me this whole time...

06:49.474 --> 06:50.994
And you found me.

06:54.774 --> 06:58.044
Well... In a way...

07:05.854 --> 07:07.114
Hup!

07:09.594 --> 07:10.854
Let's go.

07:18.204 --> 07:20.034
Kotomi! A little help, please!

07:20.034 --> 07:21.164
Yes, ma'am!

07:23.704 --> 07:24.674
Welcom-

07:25.074 --> 07:25.944
Huh?

07:25.944 --> 07:27.504
What are you doing here?!

07:28.314 --> 07:29.814
What's happened?

07:29.814 --> 07:32.574
Why are you all the way out here?
Are you by yourself?

07:33.584 --> 07:35.604
I came to pick up a friend.

07:36.314 --> 07:37.984
A friend?

07:43.654 --> 07:45.094
Miss Sato!

07:45.094 --> 07:47.494
I thought I'd seen her somewhere before.

07:47.494 --> 07:53.404
That's right, she was with you
by the wishing stones.

07:55.104 --> 07:59.604
And what? You brought Amino here?

07:59.604 --> 08:00.804
Yup.

08:03.174 --> 08:04.614
What's with you?

08:05.684 --> 08:06.734
Nothing really.

08:07.314 --> 08:10.474
I was just thinking how suddenly
you're talking like an adult.

08:11.324 --> 08:15.224
So Kara- Miss Sato is up ahead this way?

08:15.894 --> 08:18.124
She sure is funny, isn't she?

08:19.364 --> 08:23.524
She said that the wishing stones
turned her into an adult.

08:26.104 --> 08:30.304
The thing is, someone else
who was an adult became a child.

08:33.274 --> 08:37.284
And maybe that other person is you.

08:37.284 --> 08:38.874
It is.

08:42.984 --> 08:43.614
LOOKOUT

08:43.614 --> 08:45.084
LOOKOUT
Up there, right?

08:45.084 --> 08:47.754
LOOKOUT
Thank you. This is far enough.

08:47.754 --> 08:48.814
LOOKOUT

09:06.044 --> 09:07.304
Karada.

09:09.874 --> 09:12.404
Miss Shoko! How did you?

09:14.284 --> 09:16.304
You told me yourself, didn't you?

09:16.614 --> 09:19.854
You said you were at the volleyball
and swimming tube place.

09:22.524 --> 09:25.964
So you've been keeping this
great scenery all to yourself...

09:37.204 --> 09:38.934
I ran into Amino.

09:40.844 --> 09:42.574
It must've been hard for you.

09:46.314 --> 09:48.974
You love him, don't you?

10:09.704 --> 10:13.004
Falling in love with someone
is a wonderful thing.

10:14.514 --> 10:20.974
Even if it leads to heartache... or to hardship.

10:24.354 --> 10:26.914
Let's go. Let's see Amino.

10:27.254 --> 10:32.124
I'll explain it to him myself,
that you really are Karada.

10:33.724 --> 10:35.724
It was Hiro, wasn't it?

10:37.964 --> 10:41.064
The person that you loved.

10:43.274 --> 10:44.534
That's right.

10:45.704 --> 10:52.584
But I... Because of me, you and he broke up.

10:53.284 --> 10:56.614
Because of my wish, you...

10:56.914 --> 10:58.974
I was able to see him again.

11:01.124 --> 11:05.214
It's because of you that I was able
to encounter Hiro again.

11:05.764 --> 11:09.784
It's because of you that we're together now.

11:10.764 --> 11:13.294
So don't be so hard on yourself.

11:13.864 --> 11:17.064
The truth is that back then, I also...

11:18.374 --> 11:19.564
Karada!

11:30.624 --> 11:31.714
Shoko!

11:33.624 --> 11:35.594
Is everything all right?

11:35.594 --> 11:38.494
I'm sorry. Karada, she...

12:00.444 --> 12:03.044
It's a lie... A lie!

12:03.514 --> 12:06.214
Miss Shoko was just being kind by saying that.

12:06.884 --> 12:10.554
Please stop being kind to me!

12:14.864 --> 12:16.994
As I thought, it's all my fault!

12:20.464 --> 12:22.734
Because I had to wish something like that!

12:23.504 --> 12:28.504
Miss Shoko became a child,
and I've been such a bother for Hiro...

12:28.674 --> 12:30.044
And for Amino!

12:30.844 --> 12:32.174
That's why...

12:34.114 --> 12:35.814
That's why I!

12:46.694 --> 12:49.294
You going somewhere again?

12:49.994 --> 12:51.264
Iokawa!

12:52.104 --> 12:53.934
Fine. Just go.

12:53.934 --> 12:57.204
But I'll search for you, again and again!

12:57.944 --> 13:00.104
And again and again, I'll find you!

13:00.774 --> 13:02.144
Amino...

13:10.014 --> 13:11.074
I love you!

13:23.034 --> 13:25.364
Thank you, Amino...

13:47.854 --> 13:51.194
What was it that you wanted to apologize for?

13:54.794 --> 13:57.964
I'm not very open.

13:57.964 --> 13:59.124
I know.

14:00.364 --> 14:04.494
I've been that way since I was a kid.
I didn't even have any friends.

14:05.344 --> 14:09.364
That's right. Not even when I met you...

14:11.014 --> 14:16.344
By the time I moved to Kanocho,
I'd grown sick of everything.

14:17.484 --> 14:20.184
Always dragging around
the skeletons of the past...

14:21.654 --> 14:26.564
I'd even started to think that getting
dumped by you was my own fault.

14:27.494 --> 14:30.554
That's when I met her.

14:32.504 --> 14:35.564
I'm sure I made a wish of my own.

14:36.704 --> 14:38.934
That I wanted to return to my childhood...

14:39.874 --> 14:44.744
To become a child like her and redo my life.

14:45.214 --> 14:49.314
I didn't even notice I'd wished it,
but I'm sure I did.

14:52.124 --> 14:54.684
How exactly did you plan on "redoing" your life?

14:55.594 --> 14:58.824
You being you, I'm sure we still would have met.

15:02.564 --> 15:07.964
You're as cruel as always.
That's the only way you can say it?

15:09.034 --> 15:12.404
And as always, you're not being very open.

15:27.484 --> 15:29.714
Thank you for everything.

15:30.654 --> 15:33.394
Well, first and foremost,
this is a load off my mind.

15:33.394 --> 15:38.664
You've made up with Miss Sato and were even
able to find your missing classmate.

15:41.434 --> 15:46.044
Still, I didn't think you'd be taking
Miss Sato back with you!

15:46.044 --> 15:48.814
Speaking of, where is she?

15:48.814 --> 15:51.084
With her boyfriend out by the point.

15:51.084 --> 15:52.914
Don't go bothering them!

15:52.914 --> 15:54.314
Right, Tetsu?

15:55.754 --> 15:58.884
Well then, I suppose we'd better be on our way.

15:58.884 --> 16:01.294
Feel free to come back any time.

16:01.294 --> 16:02.124
Yes, ma'am.

16:02.124 --> 16:03.884
Thank you for everything.

16:07.734 --> 16:10.134
Well, there they go.

16:10.134 --> 16:13.534
Sooner or later, everyone must return home.

16:13.534 --> 16:18.904
A temporary family, a temporary haven...
That is what a bed-and-breakfast is for.

16:23.174 --> 16:24.784
Yes, hello?

16:24.784 --> 16:27.514
By the way, Shiozaki, how long will you be here?

16:27.684 --> 16:31.154
I don't know... Maybe I'll just stay forever.

16:31.154 --> 16:33.514
Kotomi! Telephone!

16:34.624 --> 16:36.154
For me?

16:36.154 --> 16:37.954
It's your father.

16:49.304 --> 16:53.044
LOOKOUT

16:54.644 --> 16:56.114
It's all right.

16:57.414 --> 17:00.244
I'm sure things are all right between them now.

17:11.324 --> 17:13.854
I'm sorry for never talking to you about it.

17:16.864 --> 17:21.324
You knew, didn't you?
That we're not really brother and sister.

17:23.004 --> 17:26.304
I never considered it a burden, not once.

17:28.474 --> 17:31.574
I enjoyed being with you.

17:32.484 --> 17:36.314
It's because you were there that I
was able to work as hard as I have.

17:40.254 --> 17:41.684
I was happy.

17:46.864 --> 17:48.554
Can I...

17:51.564 --> 17:54.904
Can I keep being your sister?

17:58.474 --> 18:01.634
Please let me keep being your brother.

18:03.014 --> 18:05.884
That's probably when it was.

18:05.884 --> 18:08.174
When my summer ended.

18:26.404 --> 18:28.234
Sasazuka
Pharmacy

18:28.234 --> 18:28.534
Sasazuka
Pharmacy
C'mon now.

18:28.534 --> 18:29.104
C'mon now.

18:29.104 --> 18:32.544
If you take this medicine,
your tummy will stop hurting.

18:33.804 --> 18:37.044
Things sure are slow.

18:37.044 --> 18:42.814
I'm glad Karada's back,
but now I've lost a lunch customer.

18:43.314 --> 18:45.984
You never had that many
customers to begin with.

18:45.984 --> 18:50.484
Aah, shut up! Who was the one who paid
for your travel expenses, huh?

18:50.794 --> 18:53.054
That's why I'm working to pay them off.

18:53.494 --> 18:59.994
By the way, you aren't looking too happy.
Even though Karada's come back.

19:00.364 --> 19:01.704
How come?

19:02.634 --> 19:03.904
Not until it's time...

19:04.744 --> 19:09.174
I'm going to get bigger.
I'm going to get bigger soon!

19:09.774 --> 19:10.974
Idiot.

19:19.084 --> 19:20.414
I'm home.

19:22.094 --> 19:23.594
Welcome back!

19:23.594 --> 19:26.194
Today's one of your favorites, a rice omelette.

19:26.194 --> 19:28.354
Sounds great.

19:29.934 --> 19:31.564
Huh? Where's Shoko?

19:31.564 --> 19:34.834
She said she had something to do,
so go ahead and eat first.

19:36.374 --> 19:38.844
Are you sure we shouldn't let the others know?

19:38.844 --> 19:43.744
It's nothing really worth mentioning.
And anyway, it's only for a little while.

19:43.744 --> 19:45.644
Then why tell just me?

19:45.644 --> 19:48.134
Why not? We're friends, right?

19:49.154 --> 19:50.984
What are you talking about?

19:50.984 --> 19:54.794
And another thing, you need to watch
how you talk to me!

19:54.794 --> 19:57.924
I may look like this, but I'm 24, you know.

19:57.924 --> 19:59.364
Yes, ma'am.

19:59.364 --> 20:02.864
If you don't know how to address people,
you'll have a hard time in the future.

20:02.864 --> 20:05.164
Don't come crying to me when
you start feeling regretful!

20:05.164 --> 20:10.264
Let's see, who was it whose life got all
tangled up about the future and regrets?

20:22.584 --> 20:25.824
My dad will get a kick out of
hearing you guys' story.

20:25.824 --> 20:27.554
Knock yourself out.

20:34.064 --> 20:34.964
Okay then.

20:34.964 --> 20:35.894
Yeah.

20:37.094 --> 20:38.464
Thank you.

20:46.604 --> 20:49.044
It's just like my dad said.

20:52.714 --> 20:54.014
Bye.

21:25.514 --> 21:27.384
Now then...

21:27.384 --> 21:29.904
Where should I begin
telling this story to my dad?

21:43.164 --> 21:44.264
Say...

21:44.264 --> 21:45.594
What?

21:45.934 --> 21:48.634
Why did you choose this city?

21:48.634 --> 21:50.194
Why did YOU?

21:51.244 --> 21:55.044
Hiro! Miss Shoko!

22:13.894 --> 22:20.134
Narenai kutsu wo haita

22:20.134 --> 22:24.864
Ippozutsu taeru itami

22:26.304 --> 22:32.584
Soredemo aruku no wa

22:32.584 --> 22:37.384
Kaeru basho ga aru kara

22:38.154 --> 22:46.294
Watashi ga watashi wo mitsumete

22:46.294 --> 22:50.894
Kizuita wasuremono

22:54.034 --> 23:00.204
Anato to issho ni itai

23:00.204 --> 23:06.914
Chikaku de, tooku de kanjitai yo

23:06.914 --> 23:12.784
Atarimae no mainichi

23:12.784 --> 23:19.424
Itoshii anato to tsukuritsuzukeru

23:19.424 --> 23:26.854
"Tadaima" to kutsu wo nuide, dakishimeru

23:27.104 --> 23:31.934
My sweet home
